hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2769","**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' ibn Kurayb, narrated to us 'Abd al-Rahim — meaning Ibn Sulayman — on the authority of Hisham ibn 'Urwah, on the authority of 'Urwah, who said:
I said to 'A'ishah (RA), ""I do not see any harm in not performing Tawaf between Safa and Marwah.""
She said, ""Why?""
I said, ""Because Allah says: 'So whoever performs Hajj to the House or performs 'Umrah, there is no blame upon him for performing Tawaf between them.' (Quran 2:158)""
She replied, ""If it were as you say, it would be otherwise. There is no blame upon him for not performing Tawaf between them. Allah only revealed this verse concerning some people of the Ansar who, in the Days of Ignorance, would consecrate themselves to Manat. Hence, it was not lawful for them to perform Tawaf between Safa and Marwah. When they came with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for Hajj, they mentioned this to him, so Allah revealed this verse. By my life, Allah does not complete the Hajj of one who does not perform Tawaf between Safa and Marwah, for Allah the Exalted says: 'Indeed, Safa and Marwah are among the symbols of Allah.' (Quran 2:158). Thus, they are among the symbols of Allah.""

Abu Bakr (a narrator in the chain) said: Her statement, ""It was not lawful for them,"" means according to their own understanding in their religion.

---"
